  "scope": [
    "Rewrite the English, Japanese, and Traditional Chinese roadmaps around user outcomes and the Console-free core operating path.",
    "Separate core maturity, evidence programs, optional tools, and future public distribution so optional surfaces do not become framework dependencies.",
    "Reconcile current Work Item truth and describe the controlled-comparison evidence without converting no-go or inconclusive samples into a success claim."
  ],
  "acceptance_criteria": [
    "All three roadmap languages share a concise outcome-based structure while reading naturally in each language.",
    "Current-state claims match canonical Work Item and Git evidence; completed, no-go, inconclusive, blocked, and deferred work remain distinct.",
    "The roadmap explains what Temple is optimizing now, how progress will be measured, what is explicitly not on the critical path, and where detailed backlog and validation records live.",
    "Management Console, Usage observation, Provider execution, and public release are presented at their real optional or deferred boundaries."
  ],
